单位就业人员指报告期末最后一日24时在本单位中工作，并取得工资或其他形式劳动报酬:
Employed persons in units refers to the number of persons working in the unit as of 24:00 on the last day of the reporting period who receive wages or other forms of labour remuneration. This is a point-in-time indicator and excludes persons whose labour contracts with the unit were terminated on or before that last day; it is the sum of staff and workers on the job, dispatched labour and other employed persons. Employed persons exclude:
(1) persons who have left the unit but retain a labour relationship with it and regularly receive living allowances;
(2) students working in their spare time and students of all kinds interning at the unit;
(3) persons used by the unit through labour outsourcing.
